Diagnose the eMMC read speed wall seen during the dyld shared-cache page-in:
the "ONC EMMC: rd" heartbeat now prints how long the last 8 MiB took, and the
boot-arg emmcroot_bench=<MiB> runs a timed sequential CMD17 read at the root
partition's first LBA before the HFS mount and prints KiB/s every 4 MiB.

(Patch 0107 added this file, so the base for the diff is the CI-main version,
saved as tmp/onc_emmc_before_bench.c; only bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c changes.)
--- a/bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
@@ -673,17 +673,30 @@
